    "created_at": "2015-06-12T14:57:40Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-06-12T14:57:40Z",
    "body": "I think for `replaceWith()` the new set of steps would be:\n1. Let parent be context object's parent.\n2. If parent is null, terminate these steps.\n3. Let viableNextSibling be the first following sibling not in nodes, and null otherwise.\n4. Let node be the result of converting nodes into a node.\n5. Pre-insert node into parent before viableNextSibling.\n\nAnd something similar for `before()`/`after()`. Can someone sanity check that?\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
